{
  "case_id": "2020-19-783",
  "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:36 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey L. Fisher (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The CFAA is an anti-hacking statute. It prohibits obtaining information from a computer without authorization. And to ensure comprehensive coverage, the statute also prohibits \"exceeding authorized access.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey L. Fisher (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is no overstatement to say that this construction would brand most Americans criminals on a daily basis. The scenarios are practically limitless, but a few examples will suffice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Fisher, in Musacchio versus United States, this is what we said: That statute provides two ways of committing the crime of improperly accessing a protected computer: obtaining access without authorization and obtaining access with authorization but then using that access improperly."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Okay. On your parade of horribles, a similar question to Justice Alito's, but one of your --the -- the -- the features of your parade is --is an employee checking Instagram at work. How is that obtaining or altering information?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Good morning, Mr. Fisher. Picking up on your parade of horribles, could you explain to us what the constitutional implications are of your parade?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the -- there are two constitutional problems. One are the First Amendment problems with certain applications of -- of -- of -- of the government's rule that are described in the amicus brief. Secondly, there's the vagueness problem, and that's what I'll focus on."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Good afternoon, Mr. Fisher. We've been focusing on the \"exceeds authorized access\" prong, you know, which is the prong that mattered for Mr. Van Buren. But I want to ask you how that prong relates to the other prong, the \"accesses a computer without authorization\" prohibition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I have two, Your Honor. Number one -- and I'm happy to get into this -- I don't think there's --this is a grievously ambiguous statute or even an ambiguous one. I think it clearly supports us, and his reading is textually insupportable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: No? Why not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Don't you think your -- Mr. Feigin, doesn't your reading sort of render superfluous the second part of the statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The word \"so\" here really does ensure that this is covering the kind of conduct that Congress wanted to cover."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FEIGIN: Well, Your Honor, I don't think that -- I don't think that's the kind of authorization the statute's referring to. It's talking about authorization by the owner of the computer data, not just some external constraint that's placed on anybody."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think what the Court should not do is to interpret this particular portion of the statute in an atextual manner that's different from how the Court viewed the plain language in Musacchio in order to avoid a parade"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, as to the text, I don't think it matters if Mr. Feigin said whether \"so\" refers strictly to accessing the computer with authorization or whether it refers to such access. Either way, it's referring to the manner of getting the information, which is by computer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The second textual point is about the word \"authorization.\" The government clearly is putting an enormous amount of weight on that term in this statute. But there's just very serious problems with that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-783",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "document_hash": "765aff5c1e323b4d2ec871721e65b6390eead0606bd0a3489a410d1e45770186",
      "evidence_id": "ev-765aff5c1e32-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
